source: crates/lobo-cli/tests/help_parity.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8(output).unwrap()"
---
Set keys in the config file. KEY= removes a key. With --stdin, reads one JSON object
{"KEY": "value"} from stdin instead, so secrets never show up in the process list.

Usage:
  lobo config set [OPTIONS] [KEY=value]...

Arguments:
  [KEY=value]...
          

Flags:
      --stdin[=<STDIN>]
          read {"KEY": "value"} JSON from stdin (keeps secrets out of argv)

  -h, --help
          help for set

Global Flags:
      --config <string>
          config file (dotenv; the OS env is never read)
          
          [default: /home/u/.config/lobo/config.env]
